 * Official constructors (do not invent them):
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/compact/standard-library/exports
 *   circuit left<A, B>(value: A): Either<A, B>;
 *   circuit right<A, B>(value: B): Either<A, B>;
 *   The inactive side should be default<> by convention.
 * Page read 2026-10-09 shows struct field is_left (and Maybe.is_some).
 * That spelling is the Compact-repo sync midnight-docs#1387 asked for.
 * This file stays on isLeft because the support-matrix pin is Compact
 * ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23, which this lab already compiled against
 * with isLeft. Do not copy is_left from the synced page into a 0.31.1 file.
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1387
 * Kapa could not answer Either usage, and builders asked whether an
 * unbounded `>= 0.26` pragma is correct. Official examples and the
 * public-network pin use a bounded language pragma, not ledger 9.
 * Compact toolchain pin for this lab: ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * Field name on this pin is isLeft.
 * The synced docs page (read 2026-10-09) and compact#833 (compiler 0.35.0)
 * both show is_left. Do not copy that spelling into this file.
 * See docs/EITHER-FIELD-SPLIT.md.
 *
